BandcampSync is a Python module and command line script which synchronises
media purchased on a Bandcamp account with a local directory, for use with
a local media server such as Plex or Jellyfin.

Using exported session cookies it authenticates as you, indexes your
collection, downloads any purchased items missing locally, and unpacks them
into an "artist name/item title" directory tree. Downloads default to flac
where available, and a checkpoint file in the media directory keeps
subsequent runs incremental.

Both a one-shot "bandcampsync" command and a long running
"bandcampsync-service" daemon are installed.
